course: dictionary
lesson: 12411
title: Dahl: a dish and a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one you need. Dahl is one of those words. «Mum cooked a pot of dahl and we ate it with warm rice.» The pot, the cooking and the rice are clues that dahl is food.
explain: Dahl can also be a person's name. «Our teacher read us a chapter of «Matilda» by Dahl.» A book was written by someone, so Dahl here is the name of a person: the author Roald Dahl. A capital D is another clue.
explain: Always ask: what would fit here? Swap your meaning into the sentence. «We ate Roald Dahl with rice» does not make sense, so the food meaning is wrong there. Trying each meaning is a quick way to check.
fact: Dahl is a South Asian dish of split lentils, peas or beans cooked with spices into a thick stew.
fact: Dahl can also mean the dried split lentils, peas or beans themselves.
fact: Dahl, dal and dhal are different spellings of the same word.
fact: Dahl is common in Indian, Pakistani, Bangladeshi and Sri Lankan cooking, often eaten with rice or flatbread.
fact: Roald Dahl was a famous children's author who wrote «Charlie and the Chocolate Factory», «Matilda» and «The BFG». 13 September is Roald Dahl Day.
exercise: «We ate dahl with warm flatbread for tea.» What is dahl here? | *A thick stew of lentils or peas | A park in the city | A famous children's author | A type of bread
exercise: «Our class is reading «The BFG» by Dahl.» What is Dahl here? | A dish of spiced lentils | *A person's name: the author Roald Dahl | A flatbread from India | A spice you sprinkle on rice
exercise: Which word is another spelling of dahl? | lentil | *dhal | curry | Dahlia
test: «Our class is reading «Matilda» by Dahl.» What does Dahl mean here? | A type of school bag | *The children's author Roald Dahl | A dish of rice and beans | A kind of hot spice
test: Which statement about dahl is true? | Dahl is a famous children's book | *Dahl is a dish made from split lentils, peas or beans | Dahl is always eaten cold with a knife | Dahl is a type of bird
exam: Which sentence uses Dahl as a name? | Dahl was served with warm rice | Mum made a big pot of dahl for supper | We bought dahl from the market | *Our teacher read us a chapter of «Matilda» by Dahl
